      "page_idx": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.046,
            0.364,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.089,
            0.666,
            0.117
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, distance covered in 3 hours = $3 \\times { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } }$ km"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.125,
            0.319,
            0.161
          ],
          "content": "= { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } + { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } } + { \\frac { 1 } { 4 } }   \\mathrm { k m }",
          "image_source": "images/page_1_equation_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.166,
            0.254,
            0.201
          ],
          "content": "= 3 km. 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.205,
            0.559,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": "The tortoise can walk $\\frac { 3 } { 4 }$ km in 3 hours."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.241,
            0.848,
            0.28
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider a case where the time spent walking is a fraction of an hour."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.288,
            0.848,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "？ We saw that Aaron can walk 3 kilometres in 1 hour. How far can he walk in $\\frac { 1 } { 5 }$ hours?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.346,
            0.848,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": "We continue to calculate the total distance covered through multiplication."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.416,
            0.794,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": "| K | Distance in 1 hour |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\frac { 1 } { 5 }$ Distance in |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_1_table_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.554,
            0.573,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": "Distance covered in $\\frac{1}{5}$ hours $= { \\frac { 1 } { 5 } } \\times 3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.603,
            0.375,
            0.624
          ],
          "content": "**Finding the product:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.627,
            0.498,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": "Distance covered in 1 hour = 3 km."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.65,
            0.848,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": "In $\\frac { 1 } { 5 }$ hours, distance covered is equal to the length we get by dividing 3 km into 5 equal parts, which is $\\frac { 3 } { 5 }   \\mathrm { k m }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.715,
            0.438,
            0.75
          ],
          "content": "This tells us that $\\frac { 1 } { 5 } \\times 3 = \\frac { 3 } { 5 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.759,
            0.517,
            0.794
          ],
          "content": "How far can Aaron walk in $\\frac{2}{5}$ hours?"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
